 Start with `saga run main.saga`. This starter deliberately performs no physical motor/ESC output.
 
-The `drone` standard module provides attitude/rate/position control, Quad-X allocation, mission/geofence, RTL/landing/failsafe, MAVLink 2 framing/signing, and DroneCAN transport helpers. Connect real sensors/ESCs only through guarded `machine` adapters after SITL/HIL testing and with an independent hardware arming/E-stop strategy. Saga is hosted soft real-time; inner hard-real-time motor commutation and certified flight-safety functions belong on dedicated flight-control/RTOS hardware.
+The `drone` standard module provides attitude/rate/position control, Quad-X allocation, mission/geofence and explicit RTL/landing helpers, MAVLink 2 common offboard messages/framing/signing/stream parsing, and DroneCAN transport helpers. It does not automatically select RTL, LAND, or DISARM from link, battery, estimator, or geofence state.
+
+For practical flight use, prefer Saga as a companion/offboard controller connected to PX4 or ArduPilot over MAVLink. Direct ESC/motor stabilization from the hosted runtime is not qualified because Saga is soft real-time and does not provide a production EKF or hardware-timed DShot waveform backend. Connect real sensors/ESCs only through guarded `machine` adapters after SITL/HIL testing.
 """,
